    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0342" n="330" xml:id="pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94114A/3–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-19">March 19,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received March 19—11:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1662. American Interests—Far East. Legation’s 7704, November 23.<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d207-f1"/> Foreign Office note March 14 states Swiss Legation Tokyo
                    reports that since beginning 1945 it has received about dozen letters from POWs
                    detained various camps Japan.</p>
                <p>During recent visits representative Swiss Legation ascertained that POWs had been
                    informed of circular which Japanese authorities had been asked to distribute in
                    all camps regarding correspondence with protecting power.</p>
                <p>Swiss Legation not informed whether this circular also distributed camps situated
                    outside Japan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
